# Code of Conduct

The project is committed to providing a respectful, constructive, and welcoming environment for everyone participating in its standards development activities.

## Expected Behavior

Participants are expected to:

- Treat others with respect and act professionally.
- Welcome different experiences, viewpoints, and technical opinions.
- Discuss ideas and evidence rather than attacking people.
- Give constructive feedback and accept it respectfully.
- Keep discussions relevant and make room for others to participate.
- Respect privacy and avoid sharing personal or confidential information without permission.

## Unacceptable Behavior

The following behavior is not acceptable:

- Harassment, discrimination, intimidation, or personal attacks.
- Threats, abusive language, or deliberate disruption of project activities.
- Publishing someone's private information without permission.
- Repeatedly derailing discussions or preventing others from participating.
- Retaliating against someone for raising a concern or participating in a review.

## Where This Code Applies

This Code applies in project spaces, including repository issues, pull requests, discussions, meetings, and project communication channels. It also applies when someone is representing the project in a public setting.

## Reporting a Concern

Report conduct concerns privately using the contact method identified in [`GOVERNANCE.md`](GOVERNANCE.md). Do not report sensitive details in a public issue or discussion.

Include enough information to help the project understand what happened. Reports will be handled as privately as reasonably possible and shared only with people who need to respond. The project cannot promise absolute confidentiality in every circumstance.

## Responding to Concerns

The person or group designated in [`GOVERNANCE.md`](GOVERNANCE.md) will review reports fairly and take appropriate action. Depending on the circumstances, this may include a reminder of this Code, a warning, removal of content, temporary limits on participation, or removal from project activities.

Anyone handling a report who is involved in the concern or has a conflict of interest should not take part in deciding the response. Retaliation against anyone who raises a concern in good faith is not permitted.

## Scope and Questions

This Code applies to all project participants, regardless of role or repository permissions. Questions about this Code or how to report a concern may be directed through the contact method identified in [`GOVERNANCE.md`](GOVERNANCE.md).
